  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PeaceFIELD Darfur Impact Evaluation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project fills a specific data collection need in order to support the broader PeaceFIELD initiative&apos;s objective of developing new, rigorous evidence about the effectiveness of Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) - supported programming in conflict-affected areas in East and central Darfur states. IOM will conduct an end-line data collection process with support from PeaceFIELD partners at the PBF and the International Security and Development Center. The end-line data collection exercise will comprise of six activities: 1) Qualitative data collection planning and preparation; 2) First round of village visits to conduct qualitative interviews; 3) Household survey planning and preparation; 4) Training of household survey enumerators; 5) Second round of village visits to conduct the household survey and follow-up qualitative interviews; and 6) Data management, data cleaning, and handoff.</narrative>
  </description>
